AHS-009 — Orchestration Model

Document ID: AHS-009
Title: Orchestration Model
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

Architectural Views: Process, Logical

1. Purpose

This specification defines the canonical orchestration model of the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The orchestration model governs how cognitive services are coordinated, scheduled, synchronized, monitored, and managed during engineering cognition.

It separates cognitive semantics (defined by ACC and the Cognitive Pipeline) from execution mechanics, allowing different implementations to optimize runtime behavior without altering engineering meaning.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Workflow orchestration
Task scheduling
Pipeline coordination
State management
Event routing
Human interaction points
Recovery and retry behavior

This specification does not define runtime technologies, workflow engines, or messaging systems.

3. Canonical Definition

Atlas Orchestration is the coordination of cognitive activities, services, and workflows required to execute the Atlas Cognitive Pipeline while preserving its canonical semantics.

4. Objectives

The orchestration model SHALL:

Coordinate cognitive execution.
Preserve pipeline ordering.
Support asynchronous execution.
Enable parallel processing where valid.
Support human intervention.
Maintain traceability.
Recover gracefully from failures.
